    ('residential-zoning', 2, 'On the record at the Dec 2, 2025 Housing Production Strategy hearing advocating lower System Development Charges specifically for Accessory Dwelling Units and quicker implementation "to support multigenerational housing" — enabling modest, gentle-density infill (ADUs/multigenerational arrangements) within existing neighborhoods. No evidence he supports broad by-right upzoning or eliminating single-family zoning. Matches Chair 2 (allow modest density increases — duplexes, accessory units — with strong design review).', ARRAY['https://hillsboro-oregon.civicweb.net/document/254837/City%20Council%20-%2002%20Dec%202025.pdf']::text[]),
    ('climate-change', 3, 'Voted YES on Resolution No. 2911 adopting Hillsboro''s Climate Action Plan, Feb 3, 2026 (carried 4-1; official minutes: "Saba Anvery, Elizabeth Case, Rob Harris, and Cristian Salgado voted yes. Kipperlyn Sinclair voted no"). The CAP is the city''s roadmap to "reduce pollution, save energy and money, and prepare for climate impacts like extreme heat and wildfire smoke" — an invest-and-gradually-reduce framework, not an emergency ban or a 2030 fossil phase-out. Matches Chair 3 (invest in clean energy while gradually reducing reliance on fossil fuels).', ARRAY['https://hillsboro-oregon.civicweb.net/document/256729/City%20Council%20-%2003%20Feb%202026.pdf', 'https://engage.hillsboro-oregon.gov/climateplan']::text[]),
